Keeper OS @VERSION@: offer of source code
=========================================

This profile builds Keeper OS from the packages of Ubuntu 24.04 (noble), the base of Linux Mint 22, and from a few
other programs named below. Most of them are free software under the GNU General Public License (GPL), the GNU
Lesser General Public License (LGPL) and similar licences. The licence text and copyright notice of every installed
package are in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

The names Ubuntu and Xubuntu are trademarks of Canonical Ltd. and Linux Mint is a trademark of its owner. Keeper OS
is not made, approved or endorsed by Canonical or by the Linux Mint project. This image carries no Linux Mint
packages except the ones named here, and what they need that Ubuntu does not have: @MINT_PACKAGES@ ("none" means no
Linux Mint package was requested). The Linux Mint repository (http://packages.linuxmint.com, suite wilma) was only
used while building.

Where the source is
-------------------

1. Ubuntu packages. The exact package set of this image is the Ubuntu archive as it was at
   @SNAPSHOT@ (suites noble, noble-updates and noble-security). The list of packages and versions is in
   keeper-os-@VERSION@.packages.txt, delivered with the image. The source of every one of them is in the
   same archive, for example:

     https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/@SNAPSHOT@/pool/

   With apt: add "deb-src https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/@SNAPSHOT@ noble main universe" (and the
   noble-updates and noble-security suites) to a sources list, then "apt-get source <package>=<version>".

2. Linux Mint packages, if the list above names any: the source is in the Linux Mint repository
   (http://packages.linuxmint.com, "deb-src" for suite wilma) and at https://github.com/linuxmint.

3. Programs added by the build, each downloaded as an exact file (URL and SHA-256 are in tools/build-image):

     VSCodium @CODIUM_VERSION@ (MIT)        https://github.com/VSCodium/vscodium
     clangd extension @CLANGD_VERSION@ (MIT)           https://open-vsx.org/extension/llvm-vs-code-extensions/vscode-clangd
     Firefox @FIREFOX_VERSION@ (MPL 2.0 and others)  https://packages.mozilla.org/apt/ (source: https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/)
     Kotlin compiler @KOTLIN_VERSION@ (Apache 2.0)    https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin

4. Keeper OS's own parts (the agent, the image build scripts and settings, Apache 2.0):

     https://github.com/contest-keeper/ck-os

Written offer
-------------

For at least three years after you received this image, we will give you, on request, the complete
corresponding source code of any program in it that is under the GPL or LGPL, on a medium customarily used for
software exchange, for no more than the cost of doing so. Make the request at:

     https://github.com/contest-keeper/ck-os/issues

and name the image version (@VERSION@) and the program.
